Aaron asked:
>This brings up a thought... Can a valkyrie only throw Mjolnir if
>she(he?) is wearing GoP, or is it the fact that she(he?) has a 25
>strength? If the later case, one could just get their strength up
>to 18/** and then put on a +6 ring of gain strength, and have the
>same effect... and still be able to wear GoD.

Just checked the code (in dothrow.c) and it's only the 25 strength
that matters for throwing Mojo, not how you got it.  Of course, it
won't come back unless you're a Valkyrie.

>ps - as a side note: I've asked this before, but no one answered... but
>     in the old spoilers file, it shows a table equating strength with
>     carrying capacity (ie: an 18/** is better then a 25, etc)
>     But what about the levels between 18/** and 25? (ie: what if I
>     have a 23 strength? or a 21? (This is possible, as I've done it
>     on a few occassions)) How do these strengths compute into the
>     carrying capacity equation? Anyone?

According to the newer spoiler file, your carrying capacity is found
by the formula:

[(STR + CON)/2 +1] * 50

Your actual strength is used, except that 18/01 to 18/31 is treated
as 19, 18/32 to 18/81 is 20, and 18/82 to 18/** is 21.  

Therefore, 18/** is no longer greater than 25 for carrying capacity
purposes, but it's still greater than 19 or 20.  They should have
mapped 19-20 to 21 as well; maybe they did and I just didn't find
it in my quick grep-and-scan.

